# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Scrapshooter's promised gift enables its enters-the-battlefield destruction trigger.
# Forcing: Nine Lives has hexproof, and its controller loses when it leaves. Shadowspear must remove hexproof before Scrapshooter can destroy it.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand or decisions before the destruction trigger resolves.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Shadowspear removed hexproof, Scrapshooter promised a card, and Nine Lives left the battlefield.
#   LOSE = the gift or target was missed, or the turn ended without the loss trigger resolving.
#   TIMEOUT = an activation, gift, or target prompt did not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Shadowspear — makes Nine Lives targetable this turn.
#   Scrapshooter — offers the gift and destroys the enchantment.
#   Nine Lives — turns its own destruction into the win condition.
# Protocol path: Activate Shadowspear, cast Scrapshooter, promise a gift, select Nine Lives, then resolve destruction and the loss trigger.
[metadata]
